; error: 15:11: expected type ([int]@r) -> nothing, got (flex [int]@r) -> nothing; this task changes what a twofold value it is given reaches, a slice, a map or a pointer or what holds one, so it goes only where the type says 'flex' for that value, as in '(flex [int]@r) -> nothing', and nothing a fixed name owns is given to it there
; A task changing what a slice it is given reaches goes only where the task type
; says 'flex' for it: otherwise a call through the value could change what a
; fixed name owns (known bug 71).

task zero(flex xs: [int]@r)
    xs[0] = 99
fi
task apply(f: ([int]@r) -> nothing, xs: [int]@r)
    f(xs)
fi
task main()
    region r default
    fixed xs = [1, 2, ...]
    apply(zero, xs)
    show(xs)
fi
